That’s a fascinating question.

Complex numbers didn’t just add a new number. They added a hidden dimension that made previously awkward operations linear and composable. Rotation became multiplication. Oscillations became exponentials. Entire branches of physics became much cleaner.

A programming analogue might be something like this:

Program State
S = (V, C)
V = visible executable state
C = contextual/latent state

Every function becomes

f : (V,C) → (V',C')

instead of

f : V → V'

The second component isn’t metadata. It is propagated by the runtime according to algebraic rules.

